如果你愿意的话，我很乐意在播客里谈论这个。

00:03:04.889 --> 00:03:07.129
I'm happy to talk about it on the podcast if you want.
太好了。

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:07.629
Great.
好吧，我们在录音了。

00:03:07.629 --> 00:03:08.541
Well, we're recording.
那我们开始吧。

00:03:08.289 --> 00:03:09.129
So let's get started.
哦，好吧。

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:09.669
Oh, okay.
对。

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:10.169
Yeah.
我们怎么认识的呢，是马特·博伦和杰西卡·戈尔登，我想？

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:13.770
So how we met is Matt Boren and Jessica Golden, I think?
哦，杰西卡·戈尔登，我记得杰西卡。

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.330
Oh, Jessica Golden, I remember Jessica.
你知道她现在在哪里吗，杰西卡·戈尔登？

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.169
Do you know where she is today, Jessica Golden?
她几个月前给我写过信，但提醒我一下。

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:21.729
She wrote me a couple months ago, but remind me.
不，我不知道。

00:03:21.729 --> 00:03:22.569
No, I don't know.
我很好奇。

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:23.409
I'm curious.
我好几年没见她了。

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:24.569
I haven't seen her in years.
我也没见。

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:26.169
I haven't either.
我得查查我的短信。

00:03:26.169 --> 00:03:27.889
I'll have to check my texts.
但他们带我去参加了一个聚会，你当时在某个地方当司仪。

00:03:27.889 --> 00:03:32.530
But they took me to an evening that you were emceeing somewhere.
梅尔罗斯，那里的喜剧俱乐部叫什么？

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:34.409
Melrose, what's the comedy club there?
即兴喜剧俱乐部（Improv），即兴。

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:35.729
Improv, improv.
对，即兴。

00:03:35.729 --> 00:03:37.050
Yeah, improv.
我想那是我拍《老爸老妈浪漫史》第一季结束后的第一个假期。

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:40.250
And I think it was my first season hiatus of how I met your mother.
我留着一大把长假胡须。

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.349
And I had a big long hiatus beard.
而你——对，我现在想起来了。

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:45.210
And you- Yes, it's coming back to me now.
你走到酒吧前，我说，干得好。

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:49.620
You came up to the bar and I said, great job.
你对我说出的第一句话是，你看起来像个恐怖分子，然后你就走开了。

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.620
And your first words to me, you said, you look like a terrorist and then you walked away.
但那天晚上晚些时候，我们最后还是舌吻了。

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.939
But then later that night we ended up making out.
哦，我就知道发生过什么。

00:03:56.939 --> 00:03:58.780
Oh, I knew something happened.
我很高兴我的记忆力还没完全退化。

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.139
I'm so glad my memory isn't just shot.
你知道我的意思吗？

00:04:01.139 --> 00:04:01.979
You know what I mean?
对，但那是20年前的事了，我们没有发生关系。

00:04:01.979 --> 00:04:03.900
Yeah, but it was 20 years ago and we didn't sleep together.
我确实记得这个。

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:04.740
I do remember that.
行，太好了。

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.580
Okay, great.
好吧，这是个很棒的信息。

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.020
Well, that's great information to have.
我们是在即兴俱乐部舌吻的，还是从那儿去了别的地方？

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.620
And did we make out at the improv or did we go from half a year?
不，不，不。

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:10.254
No, no, no.
你来我的小公寓呆了一小会儿，然后你不是有个室友吗？

00:04:10.254 --> 00:04:15.272
You came to my little apartment for a little while and then didn't you have a roommate?
没有。噢，好吧，我可能跟别人记混了。总之，很高兴再次见到你。

00:04:15.272 --> 00:04:20.982
No. Oh, I'm okay That I might be confusing to someone else now Anyway, it's great to see you again.
我已经好久没见你了，而你现在——你结婚了。好吧，首先你是个音乐家和演员——请原谅我之前不知道这一点，但我甚至不知道你还是个音乐家。现在这可是个很有用的信息，得传播出去。

00:04:20.982 --> 00:04:35.113
I've seen you in ages and you're now you're married Well, first of all you're a musician and an actor I mean forgive me for not knowing this but I didn't even know you were a musician Now this is great information to have and to spread the word.
他有一张新专辑叫《悼词第二卷》，所以我猜应该还有一卷《悼词第一卷》，我一有机会就要听听看。

00:04:35.113 --> 00:04:43.015
He has a new album called eulogy volume two So there's a eulogy volume one I'm assuming which I'm going to listen to as soon as possible.
没错。

00:04:43.015 --> 00:04:43.515
Correct.
对。

00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:52.686
Yeah Okay, here's a serious question Who is the more annoying group of artists as a successful actor and musician now that I know you're both Who is more sick?
好吧，有个严肃的问题：作为如今既是成功演员又是音乐家的你，哪类艺术家群体更让人烦人？

00:04:52.686 --> 00:04:53.378
Who is more?
谁更烦人？

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.604
Annoying as a group of artists Musicians or actors.
作为艺术家群体，谁更烦人？音乐家还是演员？

00:04:57.604 --> 00:05:18.959
I don't know I don't I don't think of I don't classify people by their of annoyance, but I will say that the musicians I've met, especially in Los Angeles, I now live in Brooklyn, but the musicians I met in LA and in Nashville, where I've spent a lot of time, have been incredibly generous, cool, collaborative people.
我不知道，我不会用是否烦人来给人分类，但我要说的是，我遇到过的音乐家——特别是在洛杉矶（我现在住在布鲁克林，但我以前在洛杉矶以及我呆过很长时间的纳什维尔遇到的音乐家）——都非常慷慨、酷炫、具有合作精神。

00:05:18.959 --> 00:05:28.959
Acting is maybe a little more like, mercenary, like, kind of, I don't know, but I've been doing it longer, the acting, so I'm a little more like, delighted by the newness of the music.
演戏可能稍微更功利一点，有点像——怎么说呢，但我干这行时间更长，演戏嘛，所以我对音乐带来的新鲜感感到更高兴。

00:05:28.959 --> 00:05:30.120
Do you know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.620
Absolutely, I understand what you're saying.
当然，我明白你的意思。

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:44.500
And I have to say, I have a couple of friends who are not out as musicians yet, they're working on music, but they are actors, two of them specifically that I'm thinking of, and they have the same exact sentiment.
而且我必须说，我有几个朋友还没有以音乐人的身份公开出道，他们正在做音乐，但他们其实是演员，具体我有两个这样的朋友，他们有着完全相同的感受。

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:47.860
They're going to be coming out with music, and they're both pretty big stars.
他们将要推出自己的音乐作品，而且他们俩都是挺红的明星。

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:48.860
And I had no idea.
我以前根本不知道。

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.860
I was like, wait, what, you guys?
当时我就想，等等，什么，你们俩？

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:57.420
And they're like, that's why, because we have to get it right, because we're so well-known in these other arenas, I would imagine the pressure is intense to get it right.
然后他们就说，这就是原因，因为我们必须把作品做好，由于我们在其他领域太出名了，我能想象那种必须做好的压力有多巨大。

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.459
But they said the same thing about Nashville.
但他们对纳什维尔也有同感。

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:06.819
And they also surprisingly told me that the music scene in Los Angeles is far more not adaptable.
而且他们还出人意料地告诉我，洛杉矶的音乐圈远没有那么……难以适应。

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:10.740
Like it's just there's just more going on musically in LA than New York, which surprised me.
就好像在音乐方面，洛杉矶比纽约有更多的事情正在发生，这让我很吃惊。

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:11.819
Would you agree with that?
你同意这种说法吗？

00:06:11.819 --> 00:06:12.819
That is true.
确实如此。

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:13.819
I have found New York.
我发现纽约……

00:06:13.819 --> 00:06:18.899
I think it's a matter of like the venues are just a little more like active in LA.
我觉得主要是洛杉矶的各种场馆要稍微活跃一些。

00:06:18.899 --> 00:06:26.100
So like I started playing music at the Hotel Cafe, which is like an incredibly intimate, you know, there's two stages.
所以，比如我最初是在 Hotel Cafe 开始玩音乐的，那是一个非常温馨的地方，你知道的，那里有两个舞台。

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.339
The people were so nice.
大家人都特别好。

00:06:27.339 --> 00:06:33.779
I kept getting invited to these songwriter evenings and I'd get up and do two or three songs and meet people who ended up becoming collaborators.
我不断被邀请参加那些词曲创作者之夜，然后我会上台唱两三首歌，并结识了最后成为合作伙伴的人。

00:06:33.779 --> 00:06:34.620
It was great.
那感觉真棒。

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:35.459
Yeah.
是啊。

00:06:35.459 --> 00:06:36.300
That is fun.
那挺有意思的。

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:41.699
First of all, it's so nice to not to have to do one thing, not that you have to do acting, but you know what I mean?
首先，不用只做一件事感觉太好了，倒不是说你非得去演戏，但你知道我的意思吗？

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:43.579
It's what you were saying earlier.
这就跟你刚才说的一样。

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:45.100
I feel very aligned with that.
我对此深有同感。

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:48.980
I like to get to do a lot of different things because otherwise I'll get to bored.
我喜欢尝试很多不同的事情，否则我会觉得太无聊。

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:57.180
And what I've noticed by doing a lot of things, I mean, it could be ADD or however you want to frame it, Or it could just be like artistic behavior, you know?
而且通过做很多事情，我发现——我是说，这可能是因为注意力缺陷多动障碍（ADD），或者你随便怎么定义它，也可能只是一种艺术家的行为，你知道吗？

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.660
Like the life of an artist is like, you kind of have to spread yourself around a little.
就像艺术家的生活一样，你得把自己的精力稍微分散一点。

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.019
It's not always one thing.
生活往往不只是单一的。

00:07:02.019 --> 00:07:04.459
I guess unless you're Van Gogh, it was one thing.
我想除非你是梵高，那他确实只专注于一件事。

00:07:04.459 --> 00:07:08.180
But I'm sure he had other tricks up his sleeve too, that we probably don't know about.
但我敢肯定他袖子里也藏着别的绝招，只是我们可能不知道罢了。

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:11.740
But I would say that, and then the artistry kind of bleeds into each other.
不过我要说的是，各种艺术创作会彼此交融。

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.379
Would you say that that's true?
你会觉得这是真的吗？

00:07:13.379 --> 00:07:18.779
For me, it's kind of like, I think about, there's just like different ideas need a different form.
对我来说，我觉得就像是——不同的想法需要不同的形式。

