然后我想列出10件事，而不是3件事，你知道的，今天有什么美好的事，诸如此类。

00:33:23.950 --> 00:33:25.750
So yeah, I'm all about the phones now.
所以，是的，我现在全盘拥抱手机了。

00:33:25.750 --> 00:33:26.950
I've given up.
我放弃了。

00:33:26.950 --> 00:33:31.990
We're living through the technology age and now we're living through the artificial insemination and intelligency.
我们正在经历技术时代，现在我们又在经历人工授精和人工智能时代。

00:33:31.990 --> 00:33:33.349
Don't remind us.
别提醒我们。

00:33:33.349 --> 00:33:35.309
Two things I don't want anything to do with.
这是我最不想沾边的两件事。

00:33:35.309 --> 00:33:37.509
I don't want to do it with AI.
我才不想跟AI扯上关系。

00:33:37.509 --> 00:33:39.670
Well, our next email comes from Ali.
好，我们的下一封邮件来自艾莉（Ali）。

00:33:39.670 --> 00:33:40.910
she is calling in.
她正在打电话进来。

00:33:40.910 --> 00:33:42.269
So she says, my name's Allie.
她说，我叫艾莉。

00:33:42.269 --> 00:33:46.250
I'm 32 and my brother, 31, is my best friend.
我32岁，我31岁的弟弟是我最好的朋友。

00:33:46.250 --> 00:33:49.069
Don't worry, I have other friends, like a healthy number.
别担心，我还有其他朋友，数量很健康。

00:33:49.069 --> 00:34:00.349
But for a lot of reasons, including complex family dynamics, our shared dark sense of humor and the bond we formed caring for our grandma during her dementia years, he's been the most important relationship in my life for a long time.
但由于种种原因，包括复杂的家庭动态、我们共同的黑色幽默，以及在奶奶老年痴呆期间照顾她所建立的纽带，很长一段时间以来，他一直是我生命中最重要的人关系。

00:34:00.349 --> 00:34:01.549
Here's where it gets tricky.
问题就在这里变得有些棘手。

00:34:01.549 --> 00:34:04.950
In the past year, he's entered a serious relationship.
在过去的一年里，他进入了一段认真的恋爱关系。

00:34:04.950 --> 00:34:07.910
I've known this girlfriend for years and I think she's lovely.
我认识这个女朋友好几年了，我觉得她很可爱。

00:34:07.910 --> 00:34:10.550
This isn't one of those I hate my brother's girlfriend's situations.
这不是那种“我讨厌我弟弟女朋友”的情况。

00:34:10.550 --> 00:34:12.710
Sounds like it's going to be though.
听起来倒挺像的。

00:34:12.710 --> 00:34:15.590
But something about it just isn't fully clicking for me emotionally.
但不知为什么，从情感上讲，我就是觉得有点对不上号。

00:34:15.590 --> 00:34:18.710
It's not jealousy and it's not drama, it's just change.
这不是嫉妒，也不是无理取闹，这只是改变。

00:34:18.710 --> 00:34:20.869
And apparently I'm not thriving in it.
显然我在这种状态下过得并不好。

00:34:20.869 --> 00:34:24.030
We live next door to each other because of course we do.
我们住在隔壁，因为我们当然会这么做。

00:34:24.030 --> 00:34:28.670
And I'm realizing I've built a little too much of my identity around this brother bestie dynamic.
我意识到我把太多的自我认同建立在“弟弟是最好朋友”这种动态上了。

00:34:28.670 --> 00:34:33.590
Most of my other close friends are getting married, having babies, or moving on to new life phases.
我其他的大多数密友都在结婚、生子，或者迈向人生的新阶段。

00:34:33.590 --> 00:34:38.289
And while I'm good with my own path, I think, I need more tools to invest in me again.
虽然我对自己的道路很满意，我想，我需要更多的工具来重新投资自己。

00:34:38.289 --> 00:34:46.690
So how do I begin to lovingly create space between me and my brother, who is again, still my favorite person, without feeling like I'm pushing him away?
那么，我该如何开始充满爱意地在我和弟弟之间创造一些空间——他依然是我的最爱——同时又不会觉得自己是在把他推开？

00:34:46.690 --> 00:34:48.170
I don't want to be weird or dramatic.
我不想显得怪异或戏剧化。

00:34:48.170 --> 00:34:54.650
I just want some practical, emotionally intelligent action items for carving out a little independence without breaking the bond, Allie.
我只是想要一些切合实际、富有情商的行动指南，在不破坏我们纽带的前提下，开辟出一小片独立的空间，艾莉。

00:34:54.650 --> 00:34:55.489
Hi, Allie.
嗨，艾莉。

00:34:55.489 --> 00:34:57.690
This is our special guest today, Josh Radner.
这是我们今天的特邀嘉宾，乔什·拉德纳（Josh Radnor）。

00:34:57.690 --> 00:34:58.690
Hi.
嗨。

00:34:58.690 --> 00:34:59.530
Hi.
嗨。

00:34:59.530 --> 00:35:00.369
Nice to meet you.
很高兴认识你。

00:35:00.369 --> 00:35:02.050
And that's so sweet that your best friends with your brother.
你和哥哥关系这么好，真的太甜了。

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:02.889
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

00:35:02.889 --> 00:35:03.730
That's really nice.
真的很好。

00:35:03.730 --> 00:35:09.989
I understand that you're dealing with change, but you know what, listen, this is not like everyone has problems with change.
我理解你在应对改变，但你知道吗，听着，这并不是说只有你有适应改变的问题。

00:35:09.989 --> 00:35:24.909
I mean, not everybody, but so many people have problems with change and have problems with making adjustments and actually, you know, having somebody else come in, even if your best friend wasn't your brother, it would probably be hard for you for your best friend to have a relationship and being introduced to them.
我的意思是，并不是只有你，很多人都有适应改变的问题，在调整自己以及真正让其他人融入生活时都会遇到困难，哪怕你的挚友不是你哥哥，要你去接受挚友恋爱并去接触对方，对你来说大概也是一件难事。

00:35:24.909 --> 00:35:35.070
So give yourself a little bit of grace and I would just, whatever you're into, just like exercise more of those activities, like literally, like if you're in a Pilates, make sure that you're a lotting time for that.
所以对宽容自己一点，我建议，无论你喜欢什么，就多去进行那些活动，真的，比如说如果你在上普拉提课，那就确保为此腾出充足的时间。

00:35:35.070 --> 00:35:36.969
Make sure you're a lot in time for your friends.
确保为你的朋友们也留出时间。

00:35:36.969 --> 00:35:39.489
Do you have friends, I'm assuming?
我假设你有朋友吧？

00:35:39.489 --> 00:35:40.409
I have a lot of friends.
我有很多朋友。

00:35:40.409 --> 00:35:42.070
I go to bodies every day.
我每天都去练普拉提。

